<title>CHILE: Tremor rocks Chilean capital.</title>
<headline>Tremor rocks Chilean capital.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Chilean capital of Santiago was shaken on Thursday morning by a 40 second tremor, although no damages were initially reported.</p>
<p>The rough movement was felt at 8:22 a.m. (1222 GMT), and it was strongest within the perimeter of Santiago.</p>
<p>There were no details available for its epicentre and intensity as measured on the Richter scale.</p>
<p>Alberto Maturana, head of Chile's National Emergencies Bureau, said no damages had been reported, and telephone and electric connections remained in service throughout Santiago.</p>
</text>
